+# Pinned mainnet identity checkpoint
+
+`mainnet-checkpoint-3520000-header.hex` contains the serialized Zcash mainnet header at height 3,520,000, followed by the zero transaction count used in `headers` P2P messages. The fixture records the header pinned by the production identity challenge, and regression tests verify the production hash and parent constants against these bytes.
+
+Source: CipherScan's trusted serving Zcash mainnet RPC, `getblockhash 3520000` and `getblockheader <hash> false`, observed on 2026-10-19 at 00:48:57.588 UTC. The independent header hash and parent bytes were verified locally. It had 2,682 confirmations at observation. The recorded source metadata is in `checkpoint-3520000-source.json`.
+
+Header double-SHA256 (display order): `00000000001cfe8c0d46d5f8a7f107546d56168fb5ab1cd66c8033390de10418`.
+Parent (display order): `00000000004cdd2c00f60266d185a2e0992ae8ab0a23d1896982bcf35bb720d6`.
+Proof marker: `zcash-mainnet-checkpoint-v1`.
+
+The post-fork checkpoint prevents known forks sharing Zcash's genesis and early history from qualifying. It does not demonstrate current synchronization, honest behavior, unique physical nodes, or comprehensive network discovery. A node that has not synchronized through this height remains unverified. A future fork sharing this checkpoint is outside this proof's scope; change the pin through a reviewed crawler/consumer release when needed.
+
+## Historical-origin rejection fixture
+
+`mainnet-block1-header.hex` contains the serialized Zcash mainnet block at height 1 header, followed by the zero transaction count used in `headers` P2P messages.
+
+Source: [Zebra fixture at commit `5ab556b0bdf7d6802f14ce88c2e56ce656755ce9`](https://github.com/ZcashFoundation/zebra/blob/5ab556b0bdf7d6802f14ce88c2e56ce656755ce9/zebra-test/src/vectors/block-main-0-000-001.txt). The source block's first 1,487 bytes are the header; the fixture appends `00`.
+
+Header double-SHA256 (display order): `0007bc227e1c57a4a70e237cad00e7b7ce565155ab49166bc57397a26d339283`.
+Parent (mainnet genesis, display order): `00040fe8ec8471911baa1db1266ea15dd06b4a8a5c453883c000b031973dce08`.
+
+This early header is deliberately insufficient for the current identity proof because shared-history forks can possess it. Tests reject it under mainnet P2P framing.
